    "headline": "Nezumi was originally 根 (ne, “root”, signifying somewhere hidden away) plus 住み (sumi, “to live”): “one who lives in hidden places”.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "Originally a compound of 根 (ne, “root”, more specifically signifying somewhere hidden away) + 住み (sumi, the 連用形 (ren'yōkei, “continuative or stem form”) of verb 住む sumu, “to live in a place, to reside”), meaning roughly “one who lives in hidden places”. The sumi changes to zumi as an instance of rendaku (連濁)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Abbreviation of nezumi. Used in some compounds."
      }
    ],
